      "hero_capitals": "Spelling is forgiving: accents and punctuation are ignored. Some countries split their capital — South Africa has three (Pretoria, Cape Town, Bloemfontein), Bolivia two (Sucre, La Paz), and the Netherlands governs from The Hague while Amsterdam is the constitutional capital. Those alternates are accepted.",
      "hero_continents": "The 7-continent model (US/UK): Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia, Europe, North America, South America. Many countries teach 6 (one America) or 5 (Eurasia). Here Australia and the Pacific islands are grouped as Oceania, and Antarctica has no countries. Russia and Turkey straddle two continents.",
      "hero_dist_hunt": "No score here. Slide to a distance, see which real capital-to-capital journeys are about that far, and note how confident you feel. The farthest two places on Earth can be is 20,037 km — half the circumference.",
