      "tiny_serrated_teeth_0_5_1_mm_on_the_fr": "Tiny serrated teeth (0.5-1 mm) on the front edge of each primary feather break the laminar-to-turbulent flow transition. Result: high-frequency noise scattering above prey hearing range.",
      "tiny_velvet_like_pile_0_5_mm_on_the_up": "Tiny velvet-like pile (~0.5 mm) on the upper feather surface dampens feather-on-feather friction noise during wing folding/unfolding.",
