      "hypothermia_is_core_body_temperature_d": "Hypothermia is core body temperature dropping below 95°F (35°C). It does not require ice or even cold weather — it can happen in 60°F water in summer or 50°F air in spring rain. Recognizing it early and treating it correctly is the difference between a story and a tragedy.",
